{
  "requirement": "When `output.html.git-repository-url` names a GitHub repository and `output.html.edit-url-template` uses that repository's `/edit/<branch>/{path}` form, each safely resolved source location displayed for an evidence input MUST link its repository-relative file and inclusive line range to `/blob/<branch>/<file>#L<start>-L<end>`. A source location MUST remain plain text when a safe URL cannot be derived. A generated detail page MUST use its evidence JSON file as the mdBook edit target when the file exists, or its requirement chapter when the evidence file is missing.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The sources satisfy `requirements.index.source_links`. I found no gaps in the implementation, its `{impl}` marking or the tests. I did not run the tests.\n\n**Config gating (`SourceLinks::from_config`, src/index.rs).**\n- It returns a link builder only when `output.html.git-repository-url` is `https://github.com/<owner>/<project>`. Owner and project are checked for safe characters.\n- The `edit-url-template` must be exactly `<repo>/edit/<branch>/{path}` with a non-empty branch.\n- Otherwise it returns `None`, so locations stay plain text. A template pointing at a different repository and a `javascript:` URL both give `None` in the test.\n- The blob prefix is `<repo>/blob/<branch>`.\n\n**URL derivation (`input_url`, `encode_url_segment`).**\n- The link is built as `<prefix>/<file>#L<start>-L<end>`.\n- It returns `None` for a zero start, a reversed range, absolute paths, `..` components, non-UTF-8 paths and empty paths. Each path segment is percent-encoded.\n\n**Rendering (`render_input`, `render_source_location`).**\n- Each resolved range becomes an `<a href>` wrapping the `<code>file:start–end</code>` text when a URL exists.\n- Without a URL it falls back to plain `<code>` text.\n- The href and label are HTML-escaped.\n\n**Edit target.**\n- `populate` sets the detail page's `source_path` to `evidence_edit_path` (`../evidence/<name>.json`, relative to `book.src`) when the evidence file exists.\n- Otherwise it uses the requirement's chapter path.\n- The `lib.rs` `{impl}` marker covers the matching `for_each_chapter_mut` change. It stops detail pages from being treated as definition sources now that their `source_path` points at the evidence JSON.\n\n**Tests.**\n- `source_links_use_configured_repository_and_branch` covers:\n  - a custom branch;\n  - percent-encoding of a path;\n  - rejection of `../` paths and a zero start line;\n  - `evidence_edit_path` with a nested `src`;\n  - the rendered anchor in a detail page;\n  - a mismatched repository and an unsafe URL.\n- `index_shows_evidence_states_and_links_generated_chapters` checks `source_path` for an existing evidence file (`../evidence/requirements.core.ready.json`) and for a missing one (`requirements/core.md`).\n- Plain-text fallback is exercised by other detail-page tests that pass `source_links: None`.\n\n**Minor observations, not gaps.** The branch is not URL-encoded, but it comes straight from the user's own template. A repository name of `.` or `..` would pass the character check, though it still stays on github.com.",
